    description: "**Mechanic**: The spec sentence reads \"production has dynamic f-string emits at `websocket.py`, `inheritance.py`, `di_resolution.py`\". On the current tree, only `inheritance.py:368` emits `evidence_type=f\"ast_{edge_type}\"`. The other two files contain only static-string evidence_type literals; comments at multiple lines explicitly describe how earlier f-string-style emits were folded to canonical inference labels and retired. The producer-coherence check on the live tree finds one dynamic emit total, not three.\n\n**Expectation**: The spec's evidence base for the open-enum schema posture cites only the files that actually contain the construct.\n\n**Scope**: Spec line 307; 2 of 3 cited files are documentation drift from prior refactors.\n\n**Exposure**: Any consumer reading the spec line to understand why the schema posture is open-enum and inspecting the cited files for canonical patterns.\n\n**Consequence**: The reader overstates the dynamic-emit prevalence by 3x; the open-enum justification rests on partially-fictional evidence; consumers reasoning about schema posture cannot trust the spec's count of live justifiers. (The choice of open-enum may still be correct — one dynamic emit is enough to forbid closed-enum — but the rationale is outdated.)\n\n**Source**: F60.A1 (INDEPENDENT, HIGH). Severity: Cosmetic (1).\n\nFiled via tranch 03 dogfood (passes 41-60, substrate sha256 a32c4a31..., HEAD 9a18959071). Tranch state: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dogfood_tranch_03/tranch_state.json`."  # 4369
